From 01d8f17a4c818107d36a9b217ceea3563e0be304 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:40:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 80/81] vgpu: give a sampled heap snapshot its mip levels

Component: Vulkan engine sampled images, and the draw rail's sampled heap
textures.

macOS 27's glass shaders sample the backdrop blur pyramid at an explicit
level of detail. The pyramid is a mipmapped heap texture whose levels
above 0 the guest's downsample kernel writes, and this device keeps only
level 0 (0079). Every sampled image was created with one level, so the
glass read level 0 at any LOD and was blurred far less than on a Mac.

A sampled snapshot of a mipmapped 2D heap texture now gets an image with
the texture's mip count, capped by its size. Level 0 is uploaded and each
level above is the one below halved with a linear blit, recorded with the
upload. SampledKey and SampledSlot carry the count, so a recycled image
keeps its shape.

Measured on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest at protocol 237:
85 mipmapped samples in one cold boot, no panic, and the Dock, menus and
About This Mac drawn as glass.

Verified: the reims-vgpu test suite passes, with a new test for the key;
clippy unchanged.
Not verified: the backend-metal arm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
